Or some of us grind so we look good for our friends.
But look we should not be grinding and offering up our grind to our family, or our church, or ourselves.
Worship God, not man or anything he can give.
You are serving the Lord Christ. (Colossians 3:23)
The third thing we see in this passage is that we should be transformed.
Do Not Be Conformed
When Paul talks about “the world” here, he is referring to the earthly and evil way of the world we live in.
Other translations say the “present age.”
Many of us still think of this world as our friend who just needs some help.
We should consider the ways of this age to be our enemy.
We don’t have to try in order to be influenced by the world.
They influence our thinking without us trying.
Every day we look up another state is allowing gay marriage.
They are all pressuring us to agree with them and to compromise our moral stance.
The world’s push is strong.
But we don’t have to float with the current.
Those are the ways of the world, not of God.
So for the first two chapters Paul explains deep stuff, and then he tells us how it should influence us.
But Be Transformed By The Renewing of Your Mind
And the way that we are transformed is by the renewing of our mind.
God wants us to be transformed.
It looks like putting to death what is earthly in us, and putting on God’s characteristics.
But how can we be transformed and put on Godly characteristics.
We don’t like to hear stuff like this.
Our thinking drives our doing, and our thinking needs to change.
Our flesh leans towards going with the current and it looks for opportunities to sin.
Our minds need to be renewed every single day.
We renew our minds by constantly keeping God’s way of thinking in front of us.
We desperately need God’s truth to combat those lies.
The goal of this transformation is being able to discerning the will of God.
You see that he describes the will of God as good and acceptable and perfect.
And you will be able to see that it leads you to life and to a life that pleases Him.
I’ve never been the same since.
That is worldly.
There are some of us who are full of lust and are engaging in sexual immorality.
You are conforming to the ways of the world.
We are not part of a church, so we are keeping our gifts to ourselves and not building up the body.
And if we would be transformed, we will see the goodness of God’s will. Conclusion
But those things in themselves cannot be what drive us, and they are not ultimately what we should be driven to.
We are to be driven by God’s mercy, driven to worship God, and we are to be transformed by His Word.
You say, ‘I do not repent enough.’ That is looking to yourself.
‘I am too unworthy.’ That is looking to yourself.
Every breath is a gift.
The only difference is you can make more money, but you can never make more time.”
Life is precious.
Trip is calling you to live for what counts.
If we are to rise on the Himalayan paths into the glory of God, we must know the way and not slip.
I sure cant wait to read the book Rise
But don’t forget to enjoy your time.
Do you get your pleasure from some one else’s pain.
Does holding another son on god down.
Is fixing the things that burden your life for the wrong reasons or that leave you blind.
Your testimony.
We just run because we didn’t see the depth of gods plan.
The story that never gets told.
God is coming.
And when he does we all will fear the lord because he knows what is truly right.
