Because Scripture is God-breathed it’s not: Opinion
It would be fine to treat the Bible this way if it was just a book of quotes that someone gathered together.
They’re not opinions we can choose whether or not to subscribe to.
Whatever He thinks is truth.
Because Scripture is God-breathed it’s not: Outdated
To them, it’s often offensive and in some cases downright immoral.
God’s truth does not expire.
So our job is not to ignore the stuff that doesn’t “fit us” or that doesn’t match what we think is moral.
Some of us like theology for the wrong reasons.
When you read Scripture it’s not just a history book, or just a book of wisdom, or just a book of stories.
God is speaking.
I think this is probably the sinful perspective that all of us have been guilty of at some point.
It doesn’t keep our attention.
It’s evidence of our sinful taste buds.
Let’s repent of that, trust Christ, and take advantage of the privilege to meet with God.
Because Scripture is God-breathed it’s not: Weak
It was with His Word that He created the entire Universe.
When Jesus, God the Son, came to Earth the power of His Word was on full display.
God’s Word is unimaginably powerful.
God uses His powerful Word to break into cold dead hearts and give them eyes to see Jesus, who was raised from the dead by God’s Word.
The book that sits untouched on your shelf is the Word of almighty God.
When God Himself speaks it should change the way we listen.
