I want to briefly tell you why I believe Jesus raised from the dead.
The purpose tonight is to talk about whether or not it matters, but if I’m going to insist that he actually rose and make claims based on that, I want you to know the reasons I believe it.
When you read Scripture, the Apostles don’t treat the resurrection as anything less than fact.
When the Apostles preach sermons after Jesus ascends into Heaven, they speak of the death of Jesus (which uncontested) and the resurrection of Jesus with the same force.
Scripture is clear that Jesus literally rose from the dead.
I believe it can be trusted.
And the way it’s written isn’t how you would write it if you made it up.
2.I Trust Reliable Testimony
We weren’t at the basketball game, but we trust sports announcers or friends who were there recap.
You trust them.
We weren’t at the Gettysburg address, we don’t have any footage, but we trust that it happened.
Now I know these things are different than the resurrection, but I say that to say, there are events that we believe happened because we heard about it from a reliable source.
The people who talk about the resurrection in the Bible, are as far as I can tell, reliable witnesses.
In fact, there were hundreds of eyewitnesses who saw Jesus.
I believe that testimony is overwhelming and that Jesus must have risen from the dead.
It’s the Best Explanation of the Facts
You have a Jewish man born in Galilee, teaching with a new kind of authority.
Being abandoned by his friends.
And then his tomb is found to be empty.
The disciples abandoned him.
But then when we read the book of Acts, we see that they’re all of a sudden encouraged and bold.
They teach that he’s God, to a Jewish culture, who recognizes that God is one.
So people are still around.
The authorities could have shut down the whole situation, which was a threat to them, by just showing people his body.
Thousands very soon after.
Murdered for this man.
I know I wouldn’t die for a legend that I made up.
