For I delivered to you as of first importance what I also received: that Christ died for our sins in accordance with the Scriptures, that he was buried, that he was raised on the third day in accordance with the Scriptures, and that qhe appeared to Cephas, then to the twelve.
Jesus died for our sins.
That’s part of the Gospel story.
The fact that Jesus rose from the dead confirms everything that he said about God and about himself.
That’s the claim that no other leader of any faith can or would make.
Think about the church you go to on Sunday.
Do you even hear about the death and resurrection of Christ and how it applies to our lives?
It matters for you because life is hard.
