I wish I had her sense of style.
Social media can fuel pride and keep you inwardly focused
We have to ask ourselves what our motivation really is for posting the things that we do.
Do we want to be well thought of or brag about the fun things we’ve been doing?
All of these things fuel pride and keep us focused on ourselves.
Whether you do music or have a popular blog, just because thousands of people are listening doesn’t mean everything that comes to mind is worth saying.
Do you still have deep, meaningful conversations in person?
Are you oversaturated with the details of 300 people’s lives that you’re not doing a good job of loving the 10 people you see week to week?
Knowing about someone’s life and sharing everything about your own life via social media is not the same as being a real friend.
As Jesus teaches, “My command is this: Love each other as I have loved you.
Friendship is sacrifice.
