Anyone who’s lost a loved one knows that you’ll never forget the day they passed on.
Of course, as a human race, we don’t only remember loved ones.
What’s so good about the day when the most talked about man in human history was violently beaten and killed by his enemies?
But his death is unlike any other death before it or after it .
Good Friday is good because of what Jesus accomplished through his death
But when Jesus went to the cross, He was beginning the most important part of His life’s work.
Jesus resolved to take on the sin that separated us from God, or as Paul says it, Jesus was, “making peace by the blood of His cross” (Colossians 1:20).
The day that the Son of God was put to death can be called a good day, because by it we are brought to life!
Good Friday is good because it isn’t the end of the story
Sunday morning, He was raised from the grave— full of power and glory.
If Jesus had not risen from the grave, then we could not call this “Good Friday.” If Jesus was still in the grave, I would have absolutely no hope.
He is alive and well, and He reigns supreme!
God has already shown His love for us in an unbelievable way, by giving His Son for us.
Don’t reject the lover of your soul.
Enduring Love For those of us who have believed on Him, there is nothing in the world that can ever separate us from God’s love.
So on this Valentine’s Day, take heart fam.
God loves you deeply
