Born Into His Family
But that’s not what the Bible teaches.
And the Bible teaches something even more frightening, that we’re born children of the devil.
Now many people today would say that sounds ridiculous and intolerant.
Well, yes, we’re all made by God and in that sense we’re his offspring, but the Bible means so much more when it talks about being children of God.
It’s not like being born into your family, which usually happens automatically.
But how does that happen?
Every now and then I’ll be on a plane, and I’ll ask the people next to me whether or not they have a relationship with God.
I’ll ask them what they base that on?
The verse we just read says pretty clearly, “to all who did receive him, who believed in his name, he gave the right to become children of God…” Becoming a child of God happens when you receive Jesus.
And the only thing he asks is that you receive his son by faith.
Putting your trust in Jesus.
What Is True Faith?
I know that’s what I thought.
Have you been willing to throw everything away to know Christ? New Birth
He’s saying if we’re going to be God’s children, we have to reborn.
Our old self dies.
John wants us to know that this birth is different than our first.
“Not of blood”—he wants us to know that this has nothing to do with natural descent or ancestry.
“Nor of the will of man”—he wants us to know that this birth was not initiated by man.
Born again isn’t just a phrase that people came up with.
And it’s a reality that changes everything.
You’re not like everyone else anymore, so stop trying to be like them.
We also have to realize that with new birth, we’ve been adopted into a family.
Treated Like His Son
They don’t want them to feel different and awkward or like they don’t belong.
In the same way, when God adopts us as his sons and daughters, he treats us like his only begotten son, Jesus.
This is somebody whose parents are rich, and just by the fact that they were born, they’re now rich too.
Maybe they enjoy their home and their comforts, but they had to work their whole lives.
Just by nature of the fact that we’ve been reborn into God’s family, we get spiritual riches.
Jesus switched places with us.
Isn’t that amazing?
It’s like someone switched out the test results.
I know sometimes when I haven’t been in the Word the way I should be, or when I haven’t been sharing the Gospel with others like I should be, I start to feel like God is mad at me.
My sin grieves him, but my spot in his family never changes.
I really struggle with wanting everyone to think highly of me.
I’m already in good standing with him.
It’s a prison to live your life based on what other people think.
We get the abundant life—life as it was meant to be lived.
This life is not all we have.
We ignore the things that matter for eternity and chase after things that are enjoyable now.
This isn’t the best we get.
When we think this is all we get we have to do everything we can to just enjoy ourselves.
I love my son dearly.
God loves us and will give us absolutely anything that’s good for us.
We were united to Jesus, and Jesus brought us to the Father.
Question: So who can separate God’s children from Him?
My sister used to do this to me.
Well now that I have it I’m really enjoying it, and now she looks at me enjoying it and she wants it back.
Well whereas before I didn’t have any special attachment to it, now I do.
I wrote my name on it and figured out fun ways to play with it.
Now that we’re his, he claims us.
We have to remember this when we go through hard times.
