For Christians, the question is not whether or not we will face temptation, but how we will respond when we do.
God doesn’t use temptation, but he will deliver us from it if we ask.
He made it clear that he is in no way saying that it is God who tempts us but Satan, the world, and our flesh.
God uses all temptation, triumph over the temptations, and even the sins we commit for His glory.
He’s simply saying that God allows it.
If we choose to lay down our selfish desires before God and surrender to his will, a result will be a better relationship with Him, which is ultimately what he wants with us.
But God test’s us, just like he did to Abraham.
