The Perfect Anger of God — TRIP LEE - OFFICIAL SITE
On the cross, Jesus took the punishment that we deserve for the sinful lives we’ve lived.
No, we can’t forgive ourselves, but the forgiveness we need is found in Him.
Everything we need is found in Christ!
People unfairly caricature many Christians and give attention to the most ridiculous stuff.
They made it, in part, so that others would enjoy it.
What we know from Scripture is that God is a good God.
He wants us to enjoy life and praise Him for it.
I’m going to read a couple of passages that I think point this out.
So to act like he doesn’t want us to enjoy them is ridiculous.
We’ll talk more about that later.
Not five minutes or five years of pleasure, but pleasures forevermore.
Sadly we don’t always know what that looks like.
We have to trust God and His character.
There are things that you enjoy that are bad for you, things that in the long run steal joy instead of giving it.
Sometimes lying seems like it leads to fun but it harms us and others.
And as a loving act Jesus calls us to deny ourselves.
This is what it means to come after me.
God is trying to protect us.
And Jesus calls us to deny that and follow Him.
He leads us to joy.
Stop chasing the fake thing and start chasing the real thing.
We should them as a means to the end of God’s glory.
Everything is best enjoyed when it’s submitted to Christ.
But He’ll give us joy and pleasure forevermore.
