Proud Speech and the Glory of God — TRIP LEE - OFFICIAL SITE
We don’t usually care if people know we’re doing something wrong, unless it’s the authority we have to answer to.
With that in mind, I want to ask a few questions to understand the text better.
I could say rapping, but I’d rather point to awards or other achievements.
And when we do that, we take glory that belongs to God.
In the text Hannah tells us not to talk proudly, and then she tells us why: because the Lord is a God who knows and weighs deeds.
Because it’s an attack on His glory.
And if we attack His glory with proud speech, He will know.
And it’s wrong because it belongs to you.
Which is why Hannah says we shouldn’t do it.
We’d love to talk to you more about that afterwards.
We want to please our loving God.
And though we will have to answer to God for our proud speech, we should praise God that our sins are covered in Christ.
No, the sickness is what needs to be attacked.
Rejoicing in God kills both pride and hopelessness.
