]]> Today we celebrate the legacy of the foremost leader of the Civil Rights movement, Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.
Despite his youthfulness, Dr. King’s prophetic speeches and crystal clear vision led him to emerge as the leader of the movement.
He was clear on what he thought would help black people move forward, and he led others in that direction.
We can all learn from this kind of leadership.
He risked his life every time he marched, spoke, or protested.
The opposition he faced did not cloud his vision, or dampen his leadership.
