I knew it was possible that “The Good Life” was my last album, but I wasn’t sure.
I wouldn’t be out on the road with my fellow emcees as much.
I wouldn’t be a full time rapper.
Since that time, I’ve been serving at my church in Washington D.C. in various pastoral roles.
I went months without doing any shows or writing a single bar of a song because of church responsibilities.
And though I missed creating new music, I love what I’ve been doing.
My creative juices had been bottled up, and I was ready to go.
That worked out great because I could slowly craft each song, and get it as close to perfection as possible.
When I brought the idea to Gawvi he loved it, and we pushed each other to make something incredible.
But here we are over a year later, and it’s almost out!
There are many unknowns for me, but I’ll tell you what I do know:
– I still want to do music.
– I still want to write books.
Will “Rise” be my last album?
For now, I want to enjoy the moment and share with you all what I think is my best work yet.
