To please our boss or our parents or coworkers.
We can’t earn his love, but we can trust him and bring him pleasure by honoring him.
Sometimes we can be tempted to even work hard for Jesus, but to think woe is me, I work for nothing.
You work to please God, you answer to Him.
His grace motivates us to work heartily and he rewards us for the work he does in us.
I’ve seen this in my own life and been convicted by it.
I happen to be a lover of sneakers.
So a few weeks ago we had a chance to go to a great sneaker store while we were in another city and I was all excited about it.
I freaked out and was going through a lot of trouble to make it happen.
But then I stopped and asked myself, “Why?” Because I was wrapped up in it.
We find ways to make things happen.
I needed to hear this today.
‘Chase Jesus and fall in love with him until you see everything as an opportunity to tell people about Him.’
