]]> When you’re going through a hard time, people don’t always know what to say.
“Who is the liar but he who denies that Jesus is the Christ?
God directs our attention to Jesus as the Savior of the world and He doesn’t offer us any alternative paths (John 14:6, Acts 4:12).
Not Acknowledging Jesus Before Others
But we can still deny Him by being ashamed of Him before others.
We live in a culture that is increasingly hostile towards religion and specifically Christianity.
It makes Jesus look small and it’s a denial of everything that He is.
And when we stand in the presence of God unless Jesus says, “He’s with me,” we’re not getting in.
So maybe at this point you feel like you’re doing pretty good.
But any of us can live in a way that contradicts what we say.
So if your life looks like nothing has changed, something’s not right.
Our pride is a denial of God’s place as center of all things.
You words may acknowledge Jesus, but do your works deny Him?
Are you sacrificially giving yourself and your resources to others (2 Corinthians 8:1-5)?
Many of us will look at these points and see some of ourselves in one or all of them.
Even denial of God was paid for at the cross by Jesus, as we see so clearly with Peter.
