In 1 Timothy 4, Paul calls false teaching the doctrine of demons.
Jesus calls, “Come to me all you who are weary and heavy laden, and I will give you rest for your souls.” We don’t know how we’ll be delivered, but we know who can do it.
Medication can subdue us, and counseling can help us think more clearly, but only Jesus can make us whole.
So let’s try to put this into perspective.
There’s something different about this battle.
True faith shows up.
There’s no reason for fear if you are more powerful than your enemy or if you even have a chance.
What we see is a weak, defeated enemy begging for mercy.
God may allow rebellion for a time, and He may allow them to go on apart from His lordship for a moment, but Jesus WILL make all things new and He will bring all things under His feet.
He has cast out the demons.
Now he was as normal as you and me.
He didn’t deserve to be delivered.
He is loving and cares for His creation.
It may look hopeless, but we see the delivering power of Christ here.
This is the right response to an encounter with Jesus.
And when He returns He will finally defeat His enemies.
