Increased locally led actions to prepare for, respond to, and recover from disaster in Cambodia – CHF Cambodia
Under this APP, the government, local humanitarian organizations and the private sector have come together to form the Preparedness Partnership of Cambodia (PPC) in 2018 to strengthen the capacity on preparedness for emergency response in Cambodia. The PPC management group consists of National Committee for Disaster Management (NCDM), Cambodian Humanitarian Forum (CHF), and the Federation of Association for Small & Medium Enterprise of Cambodia (FASMEC).
In response to information by the APP Secretariat during the 5th APPRSC in Yangon of Myanmar, NCDM, FASMEC, and CHF conducted a series of meetings to design the Theory of Change (TOC) for PPC. The call for proposals for sub-grants under APP Phase 2 was announced on 15 January 2020.
Private Sector Network: Federation of Association of Small and Medium Enterprises in Cambodia (FASMEC)
The following are some key proposed activities in the 2-year project proposal:
NCDM/PPC also proposes to organize a National After-Action Review (AAR) workshop to reflect on actions taken during the emergency response and recovery.
NCDM proposes to deliver two trainings at the provincial level on emergency data collection for district officers in one selected province. This will facilitate implementation of the Platform for Real-time Impact and Situation Monitoring (PRISM) as a tool jointly developed by WFP which utilizes smartphones to collect and gather data during emergencies.
NCDM will also assist the PCDM in organizing a Simulation Exercise (SIMEX) in a selected province that is prone to floods.
To improve humanitarian coordination, NCDM will conduct annual national coordination meeting and PPC will organize quarterly PPC coordination meetings.
FASMEC, with the support of NCDM, will conduct a workshop to adapt the early warning system known as 1294 to all SMEs in Cambodia.
For the sustainability of PPC and locally-led actions, NCDM will organize a fundraising dialogue meeting with key humanitarian actors in the country.
FASMEC will conduct another dialogue meeting on business resilience and business continuity with its own SME groups as part of capacity-building and leveraging support.
The project will create the necessary knowledge products such as case studies on local contingency plan development, emergency assessment team, brochures/ posters/ leaflets on disaster awareness and DRM.
In terms of the reporting, the PPC country communication focal point will work closely with the APP secretariat for internal and external communications and outreach.
They will be put in the website soon.
