This vicious cycle this country is in…jaded cops targeting young black men because they fit a profile…young black men getting tired of being targeted and standing and speaking up for themselves…
Someone bitten by as dog as a child, usually grows up with an aversion to all canines…either as fear or hatred.
All my friends were black.
I got sent to the principal’s office three times that year for fighting with someone who dropped the “N-word”…IN THE 4TH GRADE…kids had already been taught to classify and look down on others….because of skin color.
It still infuriates me…I just pray instead of punch now.
My family IS the American melting pot.
A couple years ago, I went through a nasty divorce and through my own stupidity, ended up spending some time behind bars and now have a felony record.
Now, anytime a patrol car gets behind me or a cop walks past me, I am thinking, “What are they gonna do this time?
Because once they know you’re in the system…you’re a criminal for life.” And then I have to repent for being narrow minded and bigoted.
I don’t say that lightly or to take away from the gravity of your words.
There is a problem, but the black and white issue is not a black & white issue.
The problem is sin.
I thank God there are men out there right now that are obedient to His Word and are trying to help heal.
