When the belt conveyor is in use, it may encounter the problem of belt breakage, which will affect the normal operation of the conveyor. Here introduces a few tips to prevent the belt from breaking.
Pay attention to the source control of the transportation system, not let the hard and long materials enter. If necessary, crushers can be installed along the transportation system.
Pay attention to the protection of the belt and avoid the sunshine and rain. Some belts that stored for a long time should be tested for longitudinal tensile strength.
Pay attention to the belt guide grooves, cleaners and other accessories during daily maintenance. Some areas with large gaps or damage should be repaired or replaced in time.
When operating or debugging the belt conveyor, it is necessary to do a dynamic check, adjust the rollers along the line, make the conveyor does not run off when it is running.
Regularly inspect the rollers for flaw detection, so that hidden dangers such as cracks and excessive local wear can be found as early as possible to prevent further wear of the belt.
Clean up the debris accumulated near the conveyor in time, which can reduce the resistance of the conveyor and indirectly protect the belt.
Using material unloading buffer technology, it is best to use a impact bed instead of impact rollers, which can prevent large materials from penetrating the belt and causing tearing.
Reasonably design and arrange the funnel position of the belt receiving and reloading points to work better with the conveyor.
When choosing a belt conveyor, choose a good manufacturer , which can guarantee the quality of the belt, and save time and effort for subsequent repairs and maintenance.
