Various failures may occur during the entire operation of coal mine belt conveyors, check the belt conveyors on time can reduce the occurrence of these failures.
If there is excessive accumulation of bulk materials in some areas, it means that the coal mine belt conveyor has a material scattering failure. At this moment, it is necessary to check the failure situation and deal with it to prevent more serious belt production accidents.
If the buffer idler fails during operation, it will cause the belt to deviate in the direction or have difficulty in spreading materials.
If the belt is damaged during the whole process of transporting materials, and some areas are damaged, it will lead to a broken belt production accident. When the belt is damaged, be sure to cut off the damaged belt and connect it again.
Due to the long transportation interval of the coal mine belt conveyor, water may be sprinkled in some areas, which may cause the coal mine belt conveyor to deviate from the direction during operation. If not handled properly, the incorrect direction can easily cause belt production accidents.
