Internal reference method: In theory, cDNA is DNA fragments of different lengths, so the result of electrophoresis is smear. If RNA abundance is low, no product will show in electrophoresis, but this does not mean no product will be amplified by PCR.
Because internal reference has high abundance in cDNA, it is easy to amplify. If cDNA is partially degraded for various reasons, from the perspective of probability, PCR results of low abundance target genes will be greatly affected.
